-- MIKO --> Scroll position inside a bookmarked page (C13).
-- Fraction (0..1) of the bookmarked page's height that sat above the top edge of the viewport
-- when the bookmark was created. Stored as a fraction, not pixels: rotating recreates the reader
-- and re-lays out the page at a different width, so a pixel offset means nothing across
-- orientations or devices.
-- NULL means "unknown": every bookmark made before this migration, and every bookmark made in a
-- paged reading mode, where a page is never partially scrolled. Those keep opening at the top.
-- DDL kept byte-identical to page_bookmarks.sq.
ALTER TABLE page_bookmarks ADD COLUMN scroll_fraction REAL;
-- MIKO <--
